> 
> summary(est.ex)
Power Estimation Using a SFM
Recurrent events 
------------------------------------------------------------ 
Estimated power                                     : 90.21%
Maximum number of rec. events per subject           : 3
Total number of subjects                            : 400
  Experimental                                      : 200
  Control                                           : 200

Using a SFM model, a study with 400 subjects and a maximum number of 3 recurrent events per subject, will yield an estimated power of 90.21%. This design assumes a 'gap' timescale, a type-I error of 5% (2-sided), an accrual time of 0.5 time unit(s) and a follow-up time of 6 time unit(s) (follow-up until the end of study), an equal allocation ratio (1:1). Under the null hypothesis (H0), the hazard ratio is 1.0 (lack of association), whereas under the alternative (HA), it is 0.70 (30.0% risk reduction). Based on these assumptions, we anticipate approximately 719 events under H0 and 651 under HA. 

